1
00:00:35,812 --> 00:00:37,939
Looks like you've already set your sights
on someone new.

2
00:00:38,764 --> 00:00:40,710
What about your Australian dream?

3
00:00:41,266 --> 00:00:43,185
I don't think I can handle another
complicated woman, bro.

4
00:00:43,656 --> 00:00:45,157
I just got out of one, remember?

5
00:00:46,563 --> 00:00:48,941
Don't follow or get close
to Ate Ysa anymore.

6
00:00:49,398 --> 00:00:50,607
She might get worse again!

7
00:00:50,632 --> 00:00:51,550
If Bogart comes out,

8
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,343
I won't be able to
stop or calm him down.

9
00:00:53,468 --> 00:00:55,846
You can't blame Ysabelle.

10
00:00:56,096 --> 00:00:57,931
We taught her how to love.

11
00:00:59,307 --> 00:01:00,642
And how to be kind.

12
00:01:01,101 --> 00:01:02,644
That's the problem.

13
00:01:02,811 --> 00:01:05,605
Ysabelle has always
been so obedient.

14
00:01:06,314 --> 00:01:07,190
Kuya Estong?

15
00:01:07,733 --> 00:01:08,567
Yes? What is it, Yeye?

16
00:01:09,901 --> 00:01:11,069
Are we best friends now?

17
00:01:11,236 --> 00:01:14,865
Then you should sign up
to my fan club!

18
00:01:14,865 --> 00:01:16,700
And then I'll welcome you!

19
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:17,409
You'll welcome me?

20
00:01:17,409 --> 00:01:18,368
Yeah!

21
00:01:18,368 --> 00:01:20,370
Oh and then welcome to me—
to Cacainatics?

22
00:01:20,495 --> 00:01:22,497
What if your brother
triggers her again?

23
00:01:22,914 --> 00:01:24,249
It's always your brother!

24
00:01:24,583 --> 00:01:26,084
No! I don't have any accomplices.

25
00:01:26,585 --> 00:01:27,502
What painting?

26
00:01:27,586 --> 00:01:29,671
Ms. Amara texted me.
What am I going to do?

27
00:01:30,297 --> 00:01:32,048
Ate Ysa, are you okay?

28
00:01:32,549 --> 00:01:34,426
- Ysa?
- I found the painting.

29
00:02:48,684 --> 00:02:50,310
You can't take this away.

30
00:02:50,936 --> 00:02:52,354
I won't return it.

31
00:02:52,938 --> 00:02:53,934
That's mine!

32
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:57,151
Sir, that belongs to me.
I made that myself.

33
00:02:57,443 --> 00:02:59,695
Look, it says ''Ysabelle.'' That's my name.

34
00:02:59,903 --> 00:03:00,612
Are you blind?

35
00:03:01,363 --> 00:03:02,948
How do I know that's really your signature?

36
00:03:02,948 --> 00:03:04,658
That's really my signature, sir.

37
00:03:04,950 --> 00:03:08,829
Please believe me. That painting is very
important to me right now.

38
00:03:09,079 --> 00:03:09,580
No.

39
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:11,498
This is more important to me.

40
00:03:11,874 --> 00:03:15,419
Ever since I hung this up in my eatery,

41
00:03:15,753 --> 00:03:18,380
I've been getting more customers.

42
00:03:19,006 --> 00:03:21,800
Back then, only three people ate here.

43
00:03:22,217 --> 00:03:25,012
Now as you can see, we're packed.

44
00:03:25,471 --> 00:03:26,555
Wait a minute, sir.

45
00:03:26,889 --> 00:03:28,474
Could it be that your food got better?

46
00:03:28,849 --> 00:03:29,349
Right!

47
00:03:29,808 --> 00:03:30,601
No, no.

48
00:03:30,768 --> 00:03:32,019
That painting brings good luck.

49
00:03:32,519 --> 00:03:34,855
et's see how your luck turns out
once we report you to the police!

50
00:03:35,314 --> 00:03:36,774
Go ahead, then!

51
00:03:36,899 --> 00:03:39,109
I don't care!

52
00:03:39,401 --> 00:03:40,944
You'll never get this!

53
00:03:41,361 --> 00:03:42,905
Well, let's see about that, sir.

54
00:03:43,530 --> 00:03:45,157
See you at the barangay hall.

55
00:03:45,407 --> 00:03:46,366
I'll take that away from you!

56
00:03:46,533 --> 00:03:47,868
That painting needs
to be submitted already.

57
00:03:49,286 --> 00:03:50,037
Ow, it hurts!

58
00:03:50,412 --> 00:03:51,288
My heart.

59
00:03:51,663 --> 00:03:53,749
I might be having a heart attack.

60
00:03:53,874 --> 00:03:56,043
If I die, you'll be sorry.

61
00:04:13,685 --> 00:04:15,106
I'll give him a real heart attack!

62
00:04:39,795 --> 00:04:40,754
Hey, Ysabelle.

63
00:04:42,005 --> 00:04:43,423
Where's the painting
I asked you to bring?

64
00:04:44,007 --> 00:04:45,551
It looks like you don't have it.

65
00:04:47,177 --> 00:04:49,096
Ms. Amara, I'm so sorry.

66
00:04:50,347 --> 00:04:51,890
I'll completely understand if

67
00:04:51,890 --> 00:04:55,644
you won't give me another
chance or another exhibit.

68
00:04:56,061 --> 00:04:56,979
I'm really sorry.

69
00:04:57,771 --> 00:04:59,523
Why wouldn't I?

70
00:04:59,523 --> 00:05:00,148
It's because—

71
00:05:00,148 --> 00:05:02,276
Hey, hey, hey!

72
00:05:02,568 --> 00:05:04,403
It's a prank!

73
00:05:05,070 --> 00:05:06,655
Ysa pranked you, sir!

74
00:05:07,155 --> 00:05:09,283
Oh my God!

75
00:05:10,617 --> 00:05:12,077
- It's a prank!
- Wow!

76
00:05:12,077 --> 00:05:12,744
Prank.

77
00:05:12,744 --> 00:05:14,121
Fabulous!

78
00:05:14,329 --> 00:05:15,247
Is this the painting?!

79
00:05:15,247 --> 00:05:16,915
Oh, yes!

80
00:05:17,249 --> 00:05:18,292
I love it!

81
00:05:19,835 --> 00:05:20,868
Wait, how did you...

82
00:05:24,798 --> 00:05:25,774
Sir...

83
00:05:25,799 --> 00:05:28,886
Just give us the painting
because we really need it.

84
00:05:28,886 --> 00:05:31,680
What can I do? Do you want me
to wash the dishes?

85
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,931
- Sir, please!
- Wait, wait, hold on.

86
00:05:32,931 --> 00:05:34,933
Bro, help me ask for the painting.

87
00:05:34,933 --> 00:05:36,894
Please, sir! Look, I'm already on my knees!

88
00:05:36,894 --> 00:05:38,312
Sir, please! I'll do anything!

89
00:05:38,312 --> 00:05:39,438
Please, sir!

90
00:05:39,438 --> 00:05:40,939
Alright, fine! Hold on!

91
00:05:42,357 --> 00:05:43,173
There.

92
00:05:43,525 --> 00:05:44,462
You can have it.

93
00:05:46,111 --> 00:05:47,154
Well, you know.

94
00:05:48,071 --> 00:05:48,884
And also...

95
00:05:49,573 --> 00:05:51,174
How did you get here?

96
00:05:51,199 --> 00:05:52,659
How did you find this place?

97
00:05:52,826 --> 00:05:53,510
Huh?

98
00:05:53,535 --> 00:05:54,494
I asked Adel.

99
00:05:55,913 --> 00:05:56,955
There's the painting.

100
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,292
You should be happy, so smile!

101
00:06:01,585 --> 00:06:02,628
Problem solved.

102
00:06:03,879 --> 00:06:05,213
Anyway, Ysabelle.

103
00:06:06,173 --> 00:06:08,467
I'm so impressed!

104
00:06:08,717 --> 00:06:09,760
Good job!

105
00:06:09,943 --> 00:06:10,819
Thank you.

106
00:06:10,844 --> 00:06:12,137
Oh my God!

107
00:06:13,555 --> 00:06:15,265
I love it!

108
00:06:20,771 --> 00:06:22,022
I love it!

109
00:06:25,484 --> 00:06:26,693
I talked to the owner.

110
00:06:27,235 --> 00:06:28,654
I explained to him

111
00:06:29,196 --> 00:06:30,906
how much that painting means to you.

112
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:33,116
He finally agreed to return it.

113
00:06:34,826 --> 00:06:37,746
Estong, you really didn't have to do that.

114
00:06:38,789 --> 00:06:40,165
It's all right, don't mention it.

115
00:06:41,083 --> 00:06:41,959
Just...

116
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:44,252
call it even, okay?

117
00:06:46,672 --> 00:06:48,632
There. That's my son right there.

118
00:06:49,132 --> 00:06:50,676
That's my bro!

119
00:06:51,885 --> 00:06:54,471
Yay! Thank you so much!

120
00:06:54,554 --> 00:06:56,223
Really, thank you so much!

121
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:02,270
Uh...you're welcome.

122
00:07:02,354 --> 00:07:04,147
It's no big deal.

123
00:07:04,272 --> 00:07:05,065
Just happy to help you.

124
00:07:06,483 --> 00:07:08,110
All of you.

125
00:07:09,403 --> 00:07:12,906
So just take it easy, or Bogart
might come out again.

126
00:07:14,241 --> 00:07:15,200
So, are you guys close now?

127
00:07:15,659 --> 00:07:16,493
So...

128
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:18,204
you two can be friends now?

129
00:07:26,378 --> 00:07:27,508
Are we friends now?

130
00:07:31,591 --> 00:07:32,759
Uh— why not?

131
00:07:34,386 --> 00:07:35,219
Sure!

132
00:07:38,432 --> 00:07:40,017
I wish I had that too!

133
00:07:41,226 --> 00:07:42,728
Keep wishing!

134
00:07:44,521 --> 00:07:47,983
I wasn't talking about you, okay?

135
00:07:48,734 --> 00:07:49,727
Then good.

136
00:07:49,938 --> 00:07:50,821
Good.

137
00:07:51,695 --> 00:07:53,447
You? Hard pass!

138
00:07:54,281 --> 00:07:56,199
Perfect, then!

139
00:07:56,867 --> 00:07:57,753
Perfect...

140
00:07:57,779 --> 00:07:59,531
It really is a perfect match!

141
00:08:01,983 --> 00:08:02,798
Adel.

142
00:08:03,165 --> 00:08:04,391
It's getting late, let's go home.

143
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:06,110
- Alright.
- Let's go.

144
00:08:06,168 --> 00:08:07,540
- Thank you for having us.
- Oh, you guys are going now?

145
00:08:07,565 --> 00:08:09,087
- Alright, sure.
- I'll take you both home.

146
00:08:09,504 --> 00:08:10,696
You guys take care now, okay?

147
00:08:16,136 --> 00:08:16,868
Ysa?

148
00:08:17,596 --> 00:08:18,305
What's wrong?

149
00:08:18,472 --> 00:08:19,431
Are you okay, Ate?

150
00:08:19,681 --> 00:08:20,657
- Are you okay?
- Ysa?

151
00:08:20,682 --> 00:08:21,324
Hey.

152
00:08:21,349 --> 00:08:22,559
Hey! Ysa!

153
00:08:22,559 --> 00:08:23,894
- Ysa! Ysa!
- Ate! Ate!

154
00:08:23,894 --> 00:08:24,519
Ate! Ate!

155
00:08:24,519 --> 00:08:25,495
Ate Ysa!

156
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:25,979
Ate?

157
00:08:25,979 --> 00:08:26,735
Are you okay?

158
00:08:26,772 --> 00:08:27,587
Ate.

159
00:08:39,785 --> 00:08:41,180
Her condition is stable.

160
00:08:41,953 --> 00:08:43,622
Her lab results are normal,

161
00:08:43,830 --> 00:08:46,430
and her MRI showed no abnormalities.

162
00:08:46,666 --> 00:08:49,836
And I don't see any signs
of a medical emergency.

163
00:08:50,337 --> 00:08:52,881
So, does that mean Ysa's
completely fine, Doc?

164
00:08:53,215 --> 00:08:54,424
Yes, physically.

165
00:08:55,008 --> 00:08:56,802
But I'd still like to keep
her under observation,

166
00:08:57,094 --> 00:09:01,681
because I can only evaluate her
psychological state once she's fully awake.

167
00:09:02,808 --> 00:09:04,017
Doc, are you sure?

168
00:09:04,392 --> 00:09:05,936
What if suddenly...

169
00:09:06,770 --> 00:09:07,829
well, you know.

170
00:09:07,854 --> 00:09:09,231
You sure do ask a lot
of questions, don't you?

171
00:09:10,023 --> 00:09:11,650
One more question,

172
00:09:11,650 --> 00:09:14,152
and you're the one getting
a prescription from me.

173
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:17,205
Sorry, Doc. I'm just concerned.

174
00:09:17,392 --> 00:09:18,727
I know.

175
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:20,329
Just relax, Estong.

176
00:09:20,784 --> 00:09:21,993
That's normal.

177
00:09:22,244 --> 00:09:23,870
Think about it. In just two days,

178
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:26,498
she lost her painting and
searched everywhere for it.

179
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:28,959
And then she worried about the deadline.

180
00:09:29,292 --> 00:09:32,671
On top of that, her personalities
kept switching, and then,

181
00:09:32,963 --> 00:09:35,841
she suddenly got some good news.

182
00:09:36,174 --> 00:09:37,509
After so many intense emotions,

183
00:09:37,509 --> 00:09:39,803
sometimes the body just decides
to shut down and rest.

184
00:09:40,804 --> 00:09:42,764
Like a reset, Doc?

185
00:09:43,431 --> 00:09:44,641
Something like that.

186
00:09:45,142 --> 00:09:47,769
The mind protects itself
the best way it knows how.

187
00:09:48,228 --> 00:09:50,313
Doc, what do we need to do?

188
00:09:50,856 --> 00:09:52,649
Let's just let her rest.

189
00:09:52,941 --> 00:09:55,110
She most likely just
entered her inner world.

190
00:09:57,946 --> 00:09:59,156
Inner world?

191
00:10:01,032 --> 00:10:05,078
In Ysa's case, she has created
a world inside her mind.

192
00:10:05,495 --> 00:10:07,455
Based on Ysa's description...

193
00:10:08,456 --> 00:10:11,042
this looks like the house she grew up in.

194
00:10:11,376 --> 00:10:12,627
Only safer.

195
00:10:23,471 --> 00:10:27,392
Whenever a personality takes over, that's
usually where Ysa goes,

196
00:10:27,392 --> 00:10:29,311
and the other personalities are also there.

197
00:10:30,896 --> 00:10:32,772
Sometimes they're all in the same place,

198
00:10:32,981 --> 00:10:34,399
but usually

199
00:10:34,691 --> 00:10:35,709
they mind their own business.

200
00:10:35,734 --> 00:10:37,110
They're separate entities.

201
00:10:37,319 --> 00:10:40,530
Especially when the personalities
don't get along.

202
00:10:41,156 --> 00:10:43,783
So they just chill there...

203
00:10:43,783 --> 00:10:45,535
like they're hanging out during break?

204
00:10:46,036 --> 00:10:46,786
Something like that.

205
00:10:47,329 --> 00:10:48,747
Sometimes they can watch
what's happening,

206
00:10:48,747 --> 00:10:50,207
sometimes they can't.

207
00:10:53,043 --> 00:10:54,753
What do they watch, Doc?

208
00:10:55,337 --> 00:10:57,672
Ysa says it's like a TV...

209
00:10:57,797 --> 00:10:59,883
like a window into reality.

210
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:03,845
If they get along with the personality
in front of them,

211
00:11:04,137 --> 00:11:08,183
they're allowed to watch what's happening
in the real world.

212
00:11:08,808 --> 00:11:10,852
If not, the window stays closed.

213
00:11:12,771 --> 00:11:13,980
So that's why...

214
00:11:14,439 --> 00:11:16,070
she sometimes forget things.

215
00:11:16,733 --> 00:11:17,776
Exactly. That's right.

216
00:11:19,861 --> 00:11:22,072
So that's why Ysa said that

217
00:11:22,405 --> 00:11:24,699
she could see everything I was doing,

218
00:11:24,699 --> 00:11:27,211
while I was with her other
different personalities.

219
00:11:27,285 --> 00:11:28,495
She said that?

220
00:11:28,995 --> 00:11:29,617
Yes.

221
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:32,485
Well, that's very good news!

222
00:11:32,874 --> 00:11:37,170
That means the personalities
are starting to cooperate.

223
00:11:37,462 --> 00:11:41,258
They're letting Ysa see
beyond the journal,

224
00:11:41,258 --> 00:11:42,842
and into their actual experiences.

225
00:11:44,177 --> 00:11:45,929
Coexistence takes time.

226
00:11:47,389 --> 00:11:49,140
Really, Doc? That's good to hear.

227
00:11:50,467 --> 00:11:54,608
Hopefully it continues. We just
need to avoid stressors and triggers.

228
00:11:54,729 --> 00:11:56,439
Doc, we'll watch over Ysa.

229
00:11:56,584 --> 00:11:57,774
Good. Very good.

230
00:11:57,774 --> 00:12:00,610
You know, I'm really
sorry, but I really have to go.

231
00:12:00,610 --> 00:12:03,154
By the way, here's the
supply of the new medication.

232
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:07,993
To help manage her symptoms,
like her anxiety and panic episodes.

233
00:12:07,993 --> 00:12:09,536
You know those very well already.

234
00:12:09,953 --> 00:12:11,014
Noted, Doc.

235
00:12:11,121 --> 00:12:15,250
Doc, thank you. I know you're busy at the
hospital, but you still came here today.

236
00:12:15,542 --> 00:12:16,751
Anything for Ysa,

237
00:12:17,711 --> 00:12:18,678
Mrs. Navarro.

238
00:12:20,505 --> 00:12:21,423
Let us walk you out.

239
00:12:21,423 --> 00:12:22,299
Okay.

240
00:12:40,608 --> 00:12:41,818
That's right, Ysa.

241
00:12:43,403 --> 00:12:44,612
You need to rest.

242
00:12:54,956 --> 00:12:55,915
Did you see that?

243
00:12:57,732 --> 00:12:58,566
You're right.

244
00:12:58,626 --> 00:12:59,737
It looks like something's going on.

245
00:13:03,548 --> 00:13:05,091
Thank you so much, Estong.

246
00:13:05,759 --> 00:13:07,844
What you did for Ysa means a lot.

247
00:13:09,116 --> 00:13:10,530
It was nothing, Tito Kent.

248
00:13:10,555 --> 00:13:13,099
No, it means a lot to us.

249
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:16,936
Do you have any intentions toward Ysa?

250
00:13:18,521 --> 00:13:19,731
Wait, Tita Barbs.

251
00:13:20,774 --> 00:13:23,526
Ysa and I became official
friends just yesterday.

252
00:13:24,194 --> 00:13:25,086
That was quick.

253
00:13:25,111 --> 00:13:26,488
But that's the thing, Estong.

254
00:13:26,863 --> 00:13:28,656
You've only just become friends,

255
00:13:28,656 --> 00:13:31,076
but the way you care
for her and smile at her...

256
00:13:32,118 --> 00:13:33,661
from the way we see it,

257
00:13:33,828 --> 00:13:35,666
it feels like you want to
take this much further.

258
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:38,166
That's how it started
with my Lovely Barbs too.

259
00:13:39,042 --> 00:13:40,085
Love at first sight.

260
00:13:41,836 --> 00:13:42,604
Love?

261
00:13:42,629 --> 00:13:45,423
Uh... I think that's
getting a little ahead, Tito.

262
00:13:45,590 --> 00:13:46,729
You know, Estong...

263
00:13:47,384 --> 00:13:49,427
Ysa has a condition,

264
00:13:49,594 --> 00:13:52,530
so we've spent her
whole life protecting her.

265
00:13:52,555 --> 00:13:55,392
There are only a few people
who truly understand her.

266
00:13:55,642 --> 00:13:58,269
Of course, we want to make sure if...

267
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:02,399
you'll have a positive effect
on her or make things worse.

268
00:14:03,983 --> 00:14:07,404
I only just moved on
from my ex, Tita, so...

269
00:14:08,405 --> 00:14:10,573
I'm not ready for a
serious relationship yet.

270
00:14:10,907 --> 00:14:11,950
Believe me.

271
00:14:12,617 --> 00:14:14,160
I only see Ysa as a friend.

272
00:14:14,327 --> 00:14:16,246
Oh! That's good to hear!

273
00:14:16,579 --> 00:14:18,915
At least we've made
things clear from the start.

274
00:14:18,915 --> 00:14:19,849
Mhm.

275
00:14:19,874 --> 00:14:22,669
And I still want to get
to know her better...

276
00:14:23,106 --> 00:14:24,149
as a friend.

277
00:14:24,379 --> 00:14:26,005
That's right, Estong.

278
00:14:26,005 --> 00:14:29,050
You should really get to know Ysa first,

279
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:31,386
and if you really do know her better,

280
00:14:32,303 --> 00:14:34,764
you should only stay as friends, okay?

281
00:14:36,349 --> 00:14:37,225
- Okay.
- Estong?

282
00:14:38,476 --> 00:14:39,511
Ysa!

283
00:14:40,061 --> 00:14:41,771
- Are you feeling better?
- Are you okay now, my dear?

284
00:14:43,022 --> 00:14:43,980
Mhm.

285
00:14:44,732 --> 00:14:46,776
Estong, thank you.

286
00:14:47,193 --> 00:14:49,320
I'm very sorry for the trouble and...

287
00:14:50,029 --> 00:14:51,739
really, thank you very much for everything.

288
00:14:52,365 --> 00:14:55,660
Oh, it's very okay and you're very welcome!

289
00:15:00,498 --> 00:15:01,875
Are you doing anything later?

290
00:15:04,127 --> 00:15:06,004
Can you paint with me?

291
00:15:06,546 --> 00:15:07,380
Um...

292
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:10,717
I have something to do later.

293
00:15:10,925 --> 00:15:11,816
Oh, I see.

294
00:15:12,302 --> 00:15:13,152
The others...

295
00:15:13,678 --> 00:15:17,599
want to learn how to paint and
they requested that you assist them.

296
00:15:19,267 --> 00:15:21,644
Uh...me? They want me to assist them?

297
00:15:22,187 --> 00:15:23,004
Mhm!

298
00:15:23,354 --> 00:15:24,981
They said they feel comfortable with you.

299
00:15:26,065 --> 00:15:27,484
But it's okay, I'll just let them know—

300
00:15:27,484 --> 00:15:29,319
- that you're busy, its okay.
- Uh no, it's really not important.

301
00:15:29,344 --> 00:15:30,360
Seriously.

302
00:15:31,488 --> 00:15:34,115
I'm free later. Just let me know what time.

303
00:15:34,449 --> 00:15:36,451
Oh no, that won't work.

304
00:15:36,618 --> 00:15:37,660
My dear, you know what,

305
00:15:37,827 --> 00:15:41,372
you have Adel or even us. We can help you.

306
00:15:41,539 --> 00:15:45,335
You know, it's better if you're
with someone they already know.

307
00:15:45,410 --> 00:15:47,496
Ninang, the others know Estong too.

308
00:15:48,046 --> 00:15:49,422
But not everyone.

309
00:15:52,884 --> 00:15:53,699
My love...

310
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:56,304
why don't we let them have this?

311
00:15:56,638 --> 00:15:57,535
Um...

312
00:15:57,805 --> 00:15:59,682
Let's just tell Estong next time.

313
00:16:01,976 --> 00:16:02,852
Tell me what?

314
00:16:02,852 --> 00:16:05,271
Oh, right. Okay, go ahead.

315
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:07,315
Alright dear, it's okay. I'll allow it.

316
00:16:18,493 --> 00:16:19,379
Come in.

317
00:16:25,583 --> 00:16:27,335
So, what was it you had to do?

318
00:16:30,797 --> 00:16:33,258
Oh, it's just paperwork for...

319
00:16:35,093 --> 00:16:36,302
Well, nothing's confirmed yet.

320
00:16:36,719 --> 00:16:38,805
But I'll let you know once it is.

321
00:16:41,015 --> 00:16:42,559
Let's manifest it!

322
00:16:42,850 --> 00:16:45,311
Whatever it is, let's
manifest that it will be certain.

323
00:16:46,938 --> 00:16:49,190
I have something to tell you too.

324
00:16:50,024 --> 00:16:50,808
What is it?

325
00:16:51,234 --> 00:16:52,777
I talked to Ms. Amara.

326
00:16:53,361 --> 00:16:56,864
She told me to make more paintings then
she'll check if

327
00:16:56,864 --> 00:16:58,491
she can include me in the exhibit!

328
00:16:59,158 --> 00:17:00,201
That's wonderful!

329
00:17:00,785 --> 00:17:01,644
Right?

330
00:17:01,828 --> 00:17:06,291
Then I'll tell the others
they should paint too.

331
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:06,958
That's right!

332
00:17:06,958 --> 00:17:09,919
It would be wonderful if we
could all be part of the exhibit.

333
00:17:11,004 --> 00:17:12,922
Their paintings should
also be approved.

334
00:17:13,423 --> 00:17:14,799
Just relax because...

335
00:17:15,341 --> 00:17:16,379
you know...

336
00:17:18,803 --> 00:17:20,513
So, where do we start?

337
00:17:20,513 --> 00:17:22,724
Uh...what can I do to help?

338
00:17:24,642 --> 00:17:27,520
Wow, exciting!

339
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,772
There's gonna be lots of food!

340
00:17:29,981 --> 00:17:31,733
Wow!

341
00:17:31,733 --> 00:17:33,610
Yes, there's going to be a
lot of food there and also...

342
00:17:33,610 --> 00:17:34,527
balloons!

343
00:17:35,445 --> 00:17:39,824
Wait, what am I gonna wear? OMG, I need
to have one tailored!

344
00:17:39,824 --> 00:17:43,369
I'll go with you, Cacai. I
know a designer. I've got you.

345
00:17:43,369 --> 00:17:47,290
OMG, I love it! Thank you so much!
Oh my gosh, I'm gonna look...

346
00:17:48,082 --> 00:17:49,792
fabulous!

347
00:17:51,044 --> 00:17:52,253
But what about me?

348
00:17:52,837 --> 00:17:55,173
I'm not good at it and
I'm not even talented.

349
00:17:55,173 --> 00:17:57,467
Uh...Ysa will teach you, Tristan. Okay?

350
00:17:57,675 --> 00:17:59,552
Just try to think positive.

351
00:18:01,792 --> 00:18:03,252
I'll try.

352
00:18:04,432 --> 00:18:06,976
If anyone starts trouble,
I'll knock them out.

353
00:18:07,453 --> 00:18:08,941
Bogart, nobody's going
to start any trouble.

354
00:18:09,437 --> 00:18:12,857
Just focus on your painting and make it
the best you can.

355
00:18:13,066 --> 00:18:15,693
Oh, of course! I'm gonna nail it.

356
00:18:15,693 --> 00:18:17,111
Okay, just relax now—

357
00:18:17,111 --> 00:18:20,907
Relax? You want me to add another bruise?

358
00:18:20,907 --> 00:18:21,816
Don't.

359
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:27,246
Oh, my. We haven't even started yet
and everyone is already making a fuss.

360
00:18:27,246 --> 00:18:28,623
No, Lola.

361
00:18:29,290 --> 00:18:31,834
Everyone's just excited. I'm excited too.

362
00:18:32,043 --> 00:18:34,629
There's nothing wrong with being excited,

363
00:18:34,796 --> 00:18:38,549
as long as everyone stays organized, okay?

364
00:18:39,175 --> 00:18:40,176
I agree, Lola.

365
00:18:42,512 --> 00:18:45,014
It's really a good thing you're here.

366
00:18:46,933 --> 00:18:48,142
Did you properly greet me already?

367
00:18:48,309 --> 00:18:49,138
Oh.

368
00:18:49,310 --> 00:18:50,353
There, sorry I forgot.

369
00:18:51,521 --> 00:18:53,815
You keep forgetting.

370
00:18:54,107 --> 00:18:54,982
I'll do better next time.

371
00:18:56,067 --> 00:18:57,110
I'll just be here, okay?

372
00:18:57,735 --> 00:18:58,778
At your service!

373
00:19:04,575 --> 00:19:05,785
Beautiful!

374
00:19:06,799 --> 00:19:09,969
It's amazing! Look at the symmetry...

375
00:19:10,206 --> 00:19:11,749
the perspective,

376
00:19:12,291 --> 00:19:16,045
the artistic "depthness."

377
00:19:16,254 --> 00:19:17,797
It's impressionist, right?

378
00:19:17,964 --> 00:19:19,173
My dear...

379
00:19:19,729 --> 00:19:22,690
"depthness" is not a word.

380
00:19:22,851 --> 00:19:23,727
Really?

381
00:19:24,137 --> 00:19:27,515
- Wow!
- It's beautiful!

382
00:19:27,515 --> 00:19:30,268
Yeye wants a medal!

383
00:19:30,268 --> 00:19:31,477
- Wow, a medal?
- Medal!

384
00:19:32,186 --> 00:19:34,814
- But it's still missing something.
- Medal!

385
00:19:34,814 --> 00:19:38,359
I think it needs something like this!

386
00:19:38,568 --> 00:19:40,737
Well, it's so beautiful
it invented a new word.

387
00:19:41,404 --> 00:19:44,240
Also, I got so impressed that's why...

388
00:19:44,949 --> 00:19:46,534
you can call me an "Impressionist."

389
00:19:46,534 --> 00:19:47,410
Shhh!

390
00:19:48,786 --> 00:19:50,246
You're so noisy.

391
00:19:50,271 --> 00:19:53,089
- It's so nice and it's so pretty.
- I know!

392
00:19:53,114 --> 00:19:54,638
Clock it!

393
00:19:55,585 --> 00:19:58,212
If there's an auction, I believe
it will get the highest bid.

394
00:19:58,212 --> 00:19:59,255
For sure!

395
00:20:02,049 --> 00:20:03,384
You're really something!

396
00:20:04,677 --> 00:20:05,887
Here's more.

397
00:20:09,515 --> 00:20:11,100
It's so pretty right?

398
00:20:12,518 --> 00:20:14,437
It's so beautiful.

399
00:20:15,396 --> 00:20:16,396
Right?

400
00:20:18,032 --> 00:20:19,325
Yes, beautiful.

401
00:20:21,944 --> 00:20:23,905
Uh...the painting. It's beautiful.

402
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,323
Oh, forget it!

403
00:20:25,823 --> 00:20:26,657
I've had enough.

404
00:20:27,617 --> 00:20:30,244
I don't know how to start
without any motivation.

405
00:20:32,622 --> 00:20:33,831
I don't know if I can do this.

406
00:20:40,129 --> 00:20:41,185
You know what,

407
00:20:42,089 --> 00:20:45,760
I know a place that can help inspire you.

408
00:20:54,811 --> 00:20:55,978
So, Tristan...

409
00:20:56,354 --> 00:20:58,272
you think you're the
only one who's creative?

410
00:20:59,774 --> 00:21:00,875
Looks great, isn't it?

411
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:02,276
My setup's great, right?

412
00:21:04,278 --> 00:21:05,488
It's very bright.

413
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:08,995
Uh...

414
00:21:09,575 --> 00:21:10,618
is it too bright?

415
00:21:11,911 --> 00:21:13,120
Fine, I'll just turn it off for now.

416
00:21:13,412 --> 00:21:14,338
No.

417
00:21:16,707 --> 00:21:17,750
I like it.

418
00:21:21,045 --> 00:21:23,881
Maybe I'm just too used to the dark,

419
00:21:26,384 --> 00:21:27,593
where there is no light.

420
00:21:31,264 --> 00:21:33,516
Maybe, I just need some light.

421
00:21:41,220 --> 00:21:42,579
To be honest,

422
00:21:44,604 --> 00:21:47,780
we see you differently from the others.

423
00:21:48,906 --> 00:21:50,491
- The artist is on the way!
- Hey, Ysa! Ysa!

424
00:21:50,491 --> 00:21:51,951
Oh, I mean... Cacai! Cacai!

425
00:21:51,951 --> 00:21:53,661
That's why...

426
00:21:53,661 --> 00:21:55,079
Yeye wants ice cream!

427
00:21:55,561 --> 00:21:57,104
we show ourselves to you more often.

428
00:21:58,291 --> 00:21:59,362
It's because

429
00:22:00,209 --> 00:22:03,254
we know you understand us.

430
00:22:08,134 --> 00:22:11,971
That's why you were the one
we chose to assist us with the paintings.

431
00:22:13,431 --> 00:22:14,393
Because...

432
00:22:16,642 --> 00:22:19,145
you bring out the best of us.

433
00:22:31,449 --> 00:22:34,160
This setup you made is
really beautiful, Estong.

434
00:22:35,244 --> 00:22:36,136
Of course.

435
00:22:37,204 --> 00:22:38,247
But...

436
00:22:39,749 --> 00:22:43,210
I think Ysa will love this more.

437
00:22:46,839 --> 00:22:49,152
Oh, Tristan, where did
you bring me this time?

438
00:22:51,427 --> 00:22:52,194
Ysa.

439
00:22:52,219 --> 00:22:53,144
Estong.

440
00:22:53,721 --> 00:22:54,597
Where are we?

441
00:22:55,473 --> 00:22:57,224
Welcome to...

442
00:22:57,391 --> 00:22:58,434
Estongville!

443
00:22:58,434 --> 00:23:00,728
So you can just sit back,

444
00:23:01,062 --> 00:23:02,772
relax and enjoy!

445
00:23:05,107 --> 00:23:06,150
Well, would you look at that.

446
00:23:11,239 --> 00:23:13,199
Looks like you've still got more in you.

447
00:23:19,872 --> 00:23:21,499
Even Tristan.

448
00:23:22,708 --> 00:23:25,503
Look, he followed what I taught him.

449
00:23:26,381 --> 00:23:27,799
It only means that...

450
00:23:28,255 --> 00:23:29,847
you're a good teacher.

451
00:23:30,258 --> 00:23:31,300
You know how to teach.

452
00:23:33,260 --> 00:23:35,346
It's also because of your efforts.

453
00:23:37,139 --> 00:23:38,516
Didn't I tell you? I can see it.

454
00:23:41,018 --> 00:23:41,727
Even though...

455
00:23:42,937 --> 00:23:45,856
sometimes, you don't know what to do,

456
00:23:47,566 --> 00:23:49,068
you're confused.

457
00:23:53,572 --> 00:23:55,372
Thank you very much, Estong.

458
00:23:56,242 --> 00:23:57,243
It's nothing.

459
00:23:58,494 --> 00:24:01,330
That's what friends are for, as they say.

460
00:24:02,081 --> 00:24:03,624
I'm also glad that...

461
00:24:04,458 --> 00:24:05,668
I got to know you even more.

462
00:24:08,504 --> 00:24:09,380
You're unfair.

463
00:24:10,798 --> 00:24:13,759
You already know so much about me, but...

464
00:24:15,803 --> 00:24:17,888
I still don't know much about you.

465
00:24:18,723 --> 00:24:19,598
Alright.

466
00:24:21,836 --> 00:24:25,431
Do you remember the first
day we met here at the café?

467
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:30,693
That was the day that I decided

468
00:24:31,402 --> 00:24:32,728
to move on...

469
00:24:33,738 --> 00:24:36,490
from the girl that I loved all my life.

470
00:24:38,753 --> 00:24:40,463
She left me because...

471
00:24:42,246 --> 00:24:44,540
she said I wasn't sure about my future.

472
00:24:49,462 --> 00:24:50,504
How about now?

473
00:24:52,048 --> 00:24:55,593
Have you figured out what
you want for your future?

474
00:24:59,972 --> 00:25:01,015
I still don't know yet.

475
00:25:03,768 --> 00:25:04,894
I feel like...

476
00:25:06,395 --> 00:25:09,273
I’m falling behind everyone else.

477
00:25:10,649 --> 00:25:11,859
So, what happened was...

478
00:25:13,194 --> 00:25:15,362
because I wanted to prove myself,

479
00:25:15,858 --> 00:25:18,235
I applied for a job abroad.

480
00:25:19,909 --> 00:25:20,910
And then,

481
00:25:21,660 --> 00:25:23,037
I got scammed by the agency.

482
00:25:24,455 --> 00:25:26,457
So now, I'm back to square one.

483
00:25:27,833 --> 00:25:28,709
That's how it goes.

484
00:25:31,754 --> 00:25:32,630
Estong.

485
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:35,950
There's nothing wrong with

486
00:25:36,592 --> 00:25:39,637
not knowing your direction in life yet.

487
00:25:44,475 --> 00:25:45,851
Just because...

488
00:25:48,562 --> 00:25:51,649
it takes you a little longer
to reach your destination,

489
00:25:52,274 --> 00:25:53,400
doesn't mean you're falling behind.

490
00:26:00,032 --> 00:26:01,408
What's important is...

491
00:26:02,470 --> 00:26:03,702
no matter what happens,

492
00:26:07,873 --> 00:26:09,375
always follow your heart.

493
00:28:54,415 --> 00:28:55,457
I figured it out, Ysa.

494
00:28:57,251 --> 00:28:57,962
Huh?

495
00:28:59,753 --> 00:29:00,860
What did your heart say?

496
00:29:03,257 --> 00:29:04,300
I now know what I want.

497
00:29:05,509 --> 00:29:06,391
Really?

498
00:29:06,677 --> 00:29:07,556
What is it?

499
00:29:09,388 --> 00:29:10,204
You.

500
00:29:14,727 --> 00:29:15,556
Me?

501
00:29:17,062 --> 00:29:18,814
You're going to teach me how to paint.

502
00:29:19,565 --> 00:29:21,317
Really? I'm going to
teach you how to paint?

503
00:29:21,567 --> 00:29:22,399
Of course!

504
00:29:22,943 --> 00:29:24,032
Why?

505
00:29:24,069 --> 00:29:25,446
Is that really what it said?

506
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:27,140
I already said yes, okay?

507
00:29:29,116 --> 00:29:30,034
Well, okay!

508
00:29:31,118 --> 00:29:32,119
I'll teach you.

509
00:29:32,578 --> 00:29:36,874
Just don't make up any new art terms, okay?

510
00:29:37,458 --> 00:29:39,501
Wow, you also saw that?

511
00:29:39,501 --> 00:29:41,337
Mhm. I watched everything.

512
00:29:42,963 --> 00:29:45,282
Next time, I'll tell them
not to make you watch.

513
00:29:54,725 --> 00:29:56,477
Look at this mess.

514
00:30:03,609 --> 00:30:04,818
- Sir, we'll be leaving now.
- Sir Boy.

515
00:30:04,985 --> 00:30:06,487
- We'll go ahead now, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

516
00:30:06,487 --> 00:30:07,696
- Sir, thank you!
- You guys take care.

517
00:30:07,696 --> 00:30:10,574
- Be safe, okay?
- Thank you so much! Bye, sir!

518
00:30:10,574 --> 00:30:13,285
- Hey, be early again tomorrow, okay?
- Yes, sir. Copy.

519
00:30:15,743 --> 00:30:16,786
Estong?

520
00:30:17,414 --> 00:30:18,373
Pops?

521
00:30:19,416 --> 00:30:22,961
The table is too shiny now,
it might blind the guests.

522
00:30:23,921 --> 00:30:25,839
Oh, I'm sorry. Is it too shiny already?

523
00:30:28,008 --> 00:30:29,802
Someone's falling in love.

524
00:30:31,212 --> 00:30:33,024
Pops, what is he trying to
say about me being in love?

525
00:30:33,180 --> 00:30:34,890
I'm not in love with Ysa, okay?

526
00:30:37,434 --> 00:30:39,853
I never mentioned any names.

527
00:30:40,145 --> 00:30:41,188
Uh...is that so?

528
00:30:42,606 --> 00:30:43,665
You know what, bro,

529
00:30:43,982 --> 00:30:46,276
there's nothing wrong
with falling in love again.

530
00:30:46,485 --> 00:30:47,694
You're single after all.

531
00:30:48,237 --> 00:30:49,446
And Ysa's also...

532
00:30:51,073 --> 00:30:52,199
Well, there are a lot of her.

533
00:30:53,909 --> 00:30:55,126
You're such an idiot.

534
00:30:55,619 --> 00:30:57,037
Bro, I'm telling you right now...

535
00:30:57,579 --> 00:30:58,831
we are only friends.

536
00:30:59,206 --> 00:31:00,235
And I'm okay with that.

537
00:31:00,457 --> 00:31:04,086
That's how it always starts. Right, Pops?

538
00:31:04,711 --> 00:31:06,088
- Estong.
- Pops?

539
00:31:06,088 --> 00:31:07,131
Are you...

540
00:31:07,589 --> 00:31:10,008
still trying to move on from your ex?

541
00:31:13,804 --> 00:31:15,722
Sometimes, I still think about it.

542
00:31:16,432 --> 00:31:17,641
But that's as far as it goes.

543
00:31:18,183 --> 00:31:21,270
I don't know, but my life
changed after I got mugged.

544
00:31:22,312 --> 00:31:24,356
I knew it, I really knew it.

545
00:31:24,648 --> 00:31:27,443
That's the day you
met Ate Ysa too, isn't it?

546
00:31:28,318 --> 00:31:29,653
Gotcha, you hairy jerk!

547
00:31:29,653 --> 00:31:32,156
One more word from
you and I'll leave you bald!

548
00:31:32,156 --> 00:31:33,031
Hey, knock it off.

549
00:31:33,031 --> 00:31:34,376
Busted!

550
00:31:34,950 --> 00:31:35,717
Pops, did you hear that?

551
00:31:35,742 --> 00:31:37,619
- That's enough.
- I got him, Pops!

552
00:31:38,162 --> 00:31:39,538
Just clean up over there.

553
00:31:40,539 --> 00:31:44,126
Alright, let's wrap this up. We
have an early day tomorrow.

554
00:31:44,126 --> 00:31:45,002
He's still not done.

555
00:31:45,002 --> 00:31:46,837
Just stop already!

556
00:31:48,630 --> 00:31:49,381
Oh my.

557
00:31:49,381 --> 00:31:50,966
You might rub the paint off.

558
00:31:58,474 --> 00:32:00,100
This should be facing front.

559
00:32:08,859 --> 00:32:10,402
He can be trusted,

560
00:32:11,111 --> 00:32:12,654
he's a kind young man…

561
00:32:13,030 --> 00:32:14,406
and he's very respectful!

562
00:32:14,740 --> 00:32:17,242
He just forgets
to greet me properly.

563
00:32:17,618 --> 00:32:20,329
I could even hear Estong
belting it out at karaoke.

564
00:32:20,954 --> 00:32:22,664
He was like a pig being slaughtered.

565
00:32:23,540 --> 00:32:26,043
That's how my heart felt too...

566
00:32:26,627 --> 00:32:29,379
slowly being slaughtered by sadness.

567
00:32:30,339 --> 00:32:31,965
Estong's full of surprises.

568
00:32:32,591 --> 00:32:34,843
He may be a wimp,
but he's got his moments.

569
00:32:37,262 --> 00:32:39,431
Yeye has a best friend now!

570
00:32:39,515 --> 00:32:41,642
I hope we can keep playing forever!

571
00:32:44,978 --> 00:32:47,105
Jestoni's got good taste...

572
00:32:47,314 --> 00:32:49,441
He really sees my beauty!

573
00:32:50,859 --> 00:32:51,883
Ysa?

574
00:32:52,486 --> 00:32:53,399
Ysa, my dear?

575
00:32:53,820 --> 00:32:54,500
Yes?

576
00:32:55,781 --> 00:32:56,579
Sweetheart...

577
00:32:57,866 --> 00:32:59,409
Why are you still awake?

578
00:33:01,912 --> 00:33:03,705
Maybe...

579
00:33:04,790 --> 00:33:07,876
someone's thinking about you, or maybe
you're thinking about someone.

580
00:33:08,293 --> 00:33:08,835
What?

581
00:33:11,547 --> 00:33:13,715
- Nonong, I'm not thinking about Esto—
- Ysa.

582
00:33:16,218 --> 00:33:17,511
You already know what it is right?

583
00:33:21,473 --> 00:33:22,266
Nanang...

584
00:33:23,433 --> 00:33:25,394
Estong and I are just friends.

585
00:33:26,353 --> 00:33:29,189
I know my boundaries. Please don't worry.

586
00:33:30,732 --> 00:33:32,901
You know, Ysa, we trust you.

587
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:34,736
But how about Estong?

588
00:33:34,903 --> 00:33:36,947
Can he control his feelings for you?

589
00:33:37,322 --> 00:33:38,532
His heart?

590
00:33:39,908 --> 00:33:40,951
Just as long as

591
00:33:41,660 --> 00:33:42,869
everything...

592
00:33:43,579 --> 00:33:44,621
will be okay.

593
00:33:46,248 --> 00:33:47,874
We're just friends, Nanang.

594
00:33:49,459 --> 00:33:50,711
Thank you, Ysa.

595
00:33:57,134 --> 00:33:58,510
Go on, get some sleep, okay?

596
00:33:59,011 --> 00:33:59,912
Don't stay up too late.

597
00:34:01,096 --> 00:34:02,139
Goodnight.

598
00:34:32,169 --> 00:34:33,295
Hey, Kuya Jim!

599
00:34:33,670 --> 00:34:35,922
- Is that my new stock?
- Oh, yes.

600
00:34:35,922 --> 00:34:36,798
You can put it down right here.

601
00:34:37,549 --> 00:34:39,968
Thank you, Kuya Jim! You're the best!

602
00:34:39,968 --> 00:34:40,761
Anytime.

603
00:34:40,761 --> 00:34:42,137
- Thank you!
- Alright.

604
00:34:42,137 --> 00:34:42,763
Take care!

605
00:34:43,722 --> 00:34:45,515
Wow, they look great!

606
00:34:46,475 --> 00:34:47,517
Wow!

607
00:34:58,195 --> 00:34:59,446
- Hello, Kuya!
- These are beautiful.

608
00:35:00,030 --> 00:35:01,239
Yes, I'm here already.

609
00:35:02,658 --> 00:35:03,700
I brought your coffee.

610
00:35:04,910 --> 00:35:06,828
Alright, Kuya. Wait a minute.

611
00:35:20,133 --> 00:35:21,343
What are you doing here?

612
00:35:23,053 --> 00:35:23,991
Delivery.

613
00:35:25,389 --> 00:35:26,598
I didn't order anything.

614
00:35:29,643 --> 00:35:30,852
This isn't for you.

615
00:35:31,144 --> 00:35:33,146
You know what, you're so full of yourself!

616
00:35:33,855 --> 00:35:35,941
This is Kuya Estong's order.

617
00:35:35,941 --> 00:35:37,275
- Oh, please.
- Just stay in your lane.

618
00:35:39,653 --> 00:35:40,629
Kuya!

619
00:35:40,654 --> 00:35:42,155
- Kuya Estong?
- These clothes are so nice.

620
00:35:42,823 --> 00:35:44,241
Kuya! Oh no—

621
00:35:45,534 --> 00:35:47,285
- What's your problem?!
- Sorry, sorry.

622
00:35:47,786 --> 00:35:49,162
My products!

623
00:35:49,162 --> 00:35:51,998
- Wait, I've got a towel. I'm gonna wipe it off.
- You spilled it on me too! You're so annoying!

624
00:35:51,998 --> 00:35:53,375
Don't you touch me.

625
00:35:53,375 --> 00:35:54,751
No, I'm gonna wipe it off.

626
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:57,045
- Oh gosh, I'm so sorry.
- How can I sell this now?!

627
00:35:57,713 --> 00:35:58,922
You spilled coffee all over it.

628
00:36:00,132 --> 00:36:01,191
I'm really, really sorry.

629
00:36:01,216 --> 00:36:02,884
- It was an accident.
- You're unbelievable.

630
00:36:02,884 --> 00:36:04,261
- Sorry.
- What do you mean it was an accident?

631
00:36:04,261 --> 00:36:06,054
You've done this before at your café.

632
00:36:06,888 --> 00:36:08,932
Déjà vu! You think I didn't notice?

633
00:36:08,932 --> 00:36:09,808
What do you mean Déjà vu?

634
00:36:10,308 --> 00:36:11,326
Hey.

635
00:36:11,351 --> 00:36:13,019
This time, I didn't mean to, okay?

636
00:36:13,019 --> 00:36:14,229
I don't believe you!

637
00:36:14,229 --> 00:36:15,622
- Hey!
- You don't believe me?

638
00:36:15,647 --> 00:36:16,608
- Kuya!
- What's going on?

639
00:36:17,441 --> 00:36:18,275
What's wrong?What's wrong?

640
00:36:18,275 --> 00:36:21,361
He ruined the clothes I was going to sell.
What am I supposed to do now?

641
00:36:21,361 --> 00:36:22,070
You need to pay for this!

642
00:36:22,428 --> 00:36:23,804
Wait a minute, I'll pay?

643
00:36:24,197 --> 00:36:25,048
- Oh, no.
- Yes!

644
00:36:25,073 --> 00:36:26,258
That's a lot!

645
00:36:26,283 --> 00:36:27,826
I don't have any money, okay?

646
00:36:27,826 --> 00:36:29,161
I can't pay for all of those!

647
00:36:29,161 --> 00:36:31,580
If you can't pay for it,
I'll just sell you instead!

648
00:36:32,038 --> 00:36:32,764
Huh?!

649
00:36:32,789 --> 00:36:34,332
We're going to do a livestream!

650
00:36:34,958 --> 00:36:36,626
You're going to sell my products online!

651
00:36:36,626 --> 00:36:37,586
Livestream?

652
00:36:38,045 --> 00:36:39,030
Oh my.

653
00:36:39,421 --> 00:36:41,923
You're only using me
to gain more followers!

654
00:36:42,215 --> 00:36:44,676
Excuse me? How dare you!

655
00:36:44,676 --> 00:36:47,095
You're the one at fault but
you're acting like you're famous!

656
00:36:47,304 --> 00:36:48,513
Well, excuse you!

657
00:36:48,764 --> 00:36:49,806
What do you mean like I'm famous?

658
00:36:50,557 --> 00:36:52,267
I just have the potential.

659
00:36:52,684 --> 00:36:54,895
Hey, hey, that's enough.

660
00:36:54,895 --> 00:36:56,730
You're being so loud.

661
00:36:57,063 --> 00:36:59,316
Ysabelle's trying to focus on her painting.

662
00:36:59,733 --> 00:37:00,817
Keep it down.

663
00:37:01,641 --> 00:37:02,683
You're so loud!

664
00:37:04,362 --> 00:37:05,217
Bro.

665
00:37:06,217 --> 00:37:08,133
Just apologize. It was your fault anyway.

666
00:37:08,306 --> 00:37:10,725
He's so annoying. He
got all the clothes wet.

667
00:37:11,620 --> 00:37:12,373
Sorry.

668
00:37:12,412 --> 00:37:13,472
What about the clothes?!

669
00:37:13,497 --> 00:37:15,624
Here we go. Here we go again, Kuya.

670
00:37:15,916 --> 00:37:16,889
It's so loud!

671
00:37:17,709 --> 00:37:18,960
It's too noisy! Be quiet.

672
00:37:20,420 --> 00:37:21,311
It's too noisy!

673
00:37:22,839 --> 00:37:23,757
You're all too noisy!

674
00:37:25,383 --> 00:37:26,301
You're all too noisy!

675
00:37:27,052 --> 00:37:28,094
Stop it!

676
00:37:31,389 --> 00:37:32,307
It's too much!

677
00:37:32,307 --> 00:37:34,518
You're all too loud! Stop it!

678
00:37:37,020 --> 00:37:40,607
OMG! My painting is really the best—

679
00:37:40,607 --> 00:37:43,819
Cacai, Ysa said my painting is the best.

680
00:37:43,819 --> 00:37:45,320
What do you mean, 'the best'?

681
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:48,114
Excuse me, my painting is the best one.

682
00:37:48,114 --> 00:37:51,243
My painting is the best, period!

683
00:37:51,243 --> 00:37:52,786
Kids...

684
00:37:53,453 --> 00:37:56,164
that's enough, kids.

685
00:37:56,164 --> 00:37:57,749
Everyone, quiet!

686
00:37:59,501 --> 00:38:03,213
You guys are quarreling again!

687
00:38:03,213 --> 00:38:06,299
Please, stop! I can't take this anymore!

688
00:38:06,299 --> 00:38:09,052
You're so loud. I'll knock
your heads together!

689
00:38:09,886 --> 00:38:12,639
Everyone, stop it!

690
00:38:12,639 --> 00:38:15,141
Stop it, please!

691
00:38:15,141 --> 00:38:17,060
- Knock it off!
- Ysa, what happened?

692
00:38:17,060 --> 00:38:19,896
They're fighting again!

693
00:38:20,605 --> 00:38:21,398
Ysa.

694
00:38:22,148 --> 00:38:23,209
Hush now, it's okay.

695
00:38:29,545 --> 00:38:32,284
Miners, mine this now!

696
00:38:32,284 --> 00:38:34,077
This is almost original!

697
00:38:34,231 --> 00:38:35,951
That's really original.

698
00:38:36,097 --> 00:38:37,681
This one's medium-sized.

699
00:38:37,706 --> 00:38:40,834
You heard that—it's a medium, for people

700
00:38:40,834 --> 00:38:41,905
with medium-sized problems.

701
00:38:42,544 --> 00:38:44,108
Come on, be serious!

702
00:38:44,462 --> 00:38:45,505
Okay, fine.

703
00:38:45,881 --> 00:38:48,800
If no one's going to buy, let's just read
some comments.

704
00:38:51,058 --> 00:38:53,560
"Mister, are you single?"

705
00:38:55,765 --> 00:38:57,726
Yes, I am very single.

706
00:38:58,341 --> 00:38:59,967
And he's going to end
up forever alone.

707
00:39:02,022 --> 00:39:04,232
Even though you really want
to "mine" me instead.

708
00:39:04,884 --> 00:39:06,510
You're always dreaming, aren't you?

709
00:39:07,819 --> 00:39:09,029
Keep dreaming.

710
00:39:09,777 --> 00:39:11,820
We have this in medium size!

711
00:39:12,504 --> 00:39:13,420
Hey.

712
00:39:13,742 --> 00:39:14,784
"Hey, you two look good together."

713
00:39:20,332 --> 00:39:21,041
No!

714
00:39:21,208 --> 00:39:23,418
- Yuck, ew, that's gross!
- Oh, no, we're not.

715
00:39:23,418 --> 00:39:24,294
Hey, knock it off.

716
00:39:24,686 --> 00:39:27,047
Maybe this will suit you
better. Are you a medium?

717
00:39:27,101 --> 00:39:28,319
You want it?

718
00:39:28,882 --> 00:39:29,674
Mine it now!

719
00:39:29,674 --> 00:39:32,677
- Mine it now. Who's a medium?.
- Mine the medium now, it's original.

720
00:39:32,844 --> 00:39:34,179
We also have something
for those who have children.

721
00:39:34,179 --> 00:39:35,305
We have a jacket here.

722
00:39:35,305 --> 00:39:36,723
If I have the money, I'll mine it.

723
00:39:36,723 --> 00:39:37,933
But it will not fit me though.

724
00:39:38,099 --> 00:39:38,975
Obviously.

725
00:39:40,352 --> 00:39:41,394
Mine this now!

726
00:39:41,394 --> 00:39:43,480
- Mine this now!
- How about this brown one?

727
00:39:43,813 --> 00:39:45,123
Something for your uncles.

728
00:39:51,613 --> 00:39:52,948
Damn it! What a waste.

729
00:39:52,948 --> 00:39:55,850
Yeye is tired of painting.

730
00:39:55,992 --> 00:39:58,828
I already feel like Tristan. Ew!

731
00:39:59,037 --> 00:40:01,598
I knew it. All my efforts were useless.

732
00:40:01,623 --> 00:40:04,376
Oh my. Those poor kids.

733
00:40:15,178 --> 00:40:16,304
Knock, knock!

734
00:40:20,308 --> 00:40:21,351
Thought you might need this.

735
00:40:24,479 --> 00:40:25,689
I do.

736
00:40:29,434 --> 00:40:30,482
Oh, uh...

737
00:40:30,652 --> 00:40:31,528
I meant the coffee.

738
00:40:31,528 --> 00:40:32,153
Uh—

739
00:40:32,153 --> 00:40:33,780
Yeah, I might need some coffee.

740
00:40:33,780 --> 00:40:34,656
Okay.

741
00:40:36,825 --> 00:40:37,701
For you.

742
00:40:39,869 --> 00:40:41,079
So...

743
00:40:43,039 --> 00:40:44,916
How's...

744
00:40:45,458 --> 00:40:46,334
everything here?

745
00:40:48,962 --> 00:40:50,672
I still haven't finished anything.

746
00:40:51,131 --> 00:40:54,009
I don't know but... this is the second time

747
00:40:54,342 --> 00:40:56,261
I've missed the deadline.

748
00:40:56,803 --> 00:40:58,096
I've been thinking that maybe...

749
00:40:58,805 --> 00:41:01,558
Maybe this exhibit just isn't meant for me.

750
00:41:02,017 --> 00:41:03,893
I can't finish this on my own.

751
00:41:09,566 --> 00:41:10,608
What's so funny?

752
00:41:13,445 --> 00:41:15,238
It just came to me that

753
00:41:16,614 --> 00:41:19,637
you'd be the last person
I'd expect to be alone.

754
00:41:20,744 --> 00:41:22,037
There are six artists here, right?

755
00:41:23,747 --> 00:41:24,956
Oh, Estong.

756
00:41:25,331 --> 00:41:26,285
No, I'm serious.

757
00:41:26,541 --> 00:41:28,084
There are a lot of you.

758
00:41:28,835 --> 00:41:30,211
Maybe you all just need

759
00:41:30,587 --> 00:41:32,547
to work together as a team.

760
00:41:48,354 --> 00:41:49,371
What?

761
00:41:50,648 --> 00:41:51,699
You're right.

762
00:41:52,776 --> 00:41:53,985
I have an idea.

763
00:41:54,652 --> 00:41:56,780
I'm sure they'll also love it.

764
00:42:07,582 --> 00:42:08,500
Good?

765
00:42:14,214 --> 00:42:16,424
There! Wait. One more.

766
00:42:17,133 --> 00:42:17,592
Ow.

767
00:42:17,592 --> 00:42:18,635
I can't reach you.

768
00:42:19,803 --> 00:42:22,138
Just hold this here, and this one too.

769
00:42:22,305 --> 00:42:25,016
Pose properly, okay?
You need to look fabulous!

770
00:42:26,059 --> 00:42:28,019
Can you lean your body a bit? Like...

771
00:42:28,186 --> 00:42:29,854
pose some more to the right.

772
00:42:30,021 --> 00:42:31,064
No, your other right.

773
00:42:31,272 --> 00:42:33,066
That's it!

774
00:42:33,483 --> 00:42:34,526
Okay, let's start!

775
00:42:35,360 --> 00:42:37,237
Hey, pose properly.

776
00:42:38,530 --> 00:42:39,906
Aren't you done yet, Yeye?

777
00:42:42,367 --> 00:42:44,411
- All done!
- You're done?

778
00:42:44,411 --> 00:42:45,620
- Mhm!
- Let me see.

779
00:42:50,708 --> 00:42:51,702
What's that?

780
00:42:54,420 --> 00:42:55,296
Is that me?

781
00:43:00,485 --> 00:43:02,278
Is it bad?

782
00:43:02,303 --> 00:43:03,346
It's good!

783
00:43:03,346 --> 00:43:06,933
- No, it's good, you even got my smile right!
- You looked like you didn't like it.

784
00:43:07,684 --> 00:43:09,748
Then the head, you got it really right.

785
00:43:10,061 --> 00:43:12,230
Look at my head, it looks like a lollipop.
You got right!

786
00:43:12,230 --> 00:43:13,273
Lollipop?

787
00:43:13,717 --> 00:43:14,941
Yes, like a lollipop.

788
00:43:16,025 --> 00:43:17,235
Lollipop?

789
00:43:17,402 --> 00:43:19,279
- Alright, let's buy you a lollipop, okay?
- Lollipop!

790
00:43:20,363 --> 00:43:21,239
I'm done.

791
00:43:22,574 --> 00:43:23,950
You're done? Let me see.

792
00:43:29,164 --> 00:43:30,373
Oh.

793
00:43:31,457 --> 00:43:33,126
This is your soul.

794
00:43:44,846 --> 00:43:45,680
I can't do this anymore!

795
00:43:45,680 --> 00:43:46,739
Why?

796
00:43:46,764 --> 00:43:47,772
It's so ugly!

797
00:43:48,808 --> 00:43:50,810
Bogart! Let's try something else!

798
00:43:52,145 --> 00:43:53,354
I don't want to do this anymore!

799
00:43:53,354 --> 00:43:55,842
- Didn't I tell you to pose properly?
- Wait, ow, ouch.

800
00:43:58,359 --> 00:44:02,989
Oh, dear, I really don't understand
kids these days.

801
00:44:03,928 --> 00:44:06,075
They've got so much going on, and..

802
00:44:06,492 --> 00:44:08,494
Cacai keeps on saying

803
00:44:09,037 --> 00:44:10,246
"clock it."

804
00:44:11,080 --> 00:44:13,583
What does "clock it" even mean?

805
00:44:13,583 --> 00:44:15,710
Is time clocking differently already?

806
00:44:16,669 --> 00:44:17,712
Oh my.

807
00:44:18,755 --> 00:44:21,549
Kids these days have really changed.

808
00:44:22,842 --> 00:44:24,385
Don't move, dear.

809
00:44:29,641 --> 00:44:30,522
Lola?

810
00:44:34,187 --> 00:44:34,959
Lola?

811
00:45:10,640 --> 00:45:12,561
Spanish Latte for...

812
00:45:12,787 --> 00:45:18,264
Lola Iska, Tristan, Bogart,
Yeye, Cacai, and...

813
00:45:18,439 --> 00:45:19,475
Ysa.

814
00:45:21,818 --> 00:45:23,111
Thank you, Estong.

815
00:45:23,736 --> 00:45:25,363
Uh...do you want some sweets?

816
00:45:25,363 --> 00:45:27,340
Pastries? Cookies?

817
00:45:27,365 --> 00:45:28,324
Cheesecakes?

818
00:45:28,658 --> 00:45:29,784
Or churros?

819
00:45:31,911 --> 00:45:33,329
No, not the churros. I don't like churros.

820
00:45:33,705 --> 00:45:35,707
No, I'm okay. Thank you.

821
00:45:36,749 --> 00:45:39,002
Well, if you need something,
just let me know.

822
00:45:39,127 --> 00:45:40,336
Okay? I'll just be here.

823
00:45:40,336 --> 00:45:43,423
I don't really need sweets.

824
00:45:44,257 --> 00:45:45,352
You're already here.

825
00:45:50,596 --> 00:45:51,723
- Uh...
- Uh...

826
00:45:52,283 --> 00:45:54,327
I just saw that from online, okay?

827
00:45:54,517 --> 00:45:56,040
- Ahhh.
- Just saying.

828
00:45:57,312 --> 00:45:59,230
So that's your thing now, huh?

829
00:46:00,064 --> 00:46:01,040
Alright. I also got one.

830
00:46:01,691 --> 00:46:02,672
Let's hear it.

831
00:46:04,360 --> 00:46:05,987
Do you know I like coffee?

832
00:46:06,654 --> 00:46:07,905
But I don't like 3-in-1.

833
00:46:08,781 --> 00:46:09,641
Huh?

834
00:46:09,782 --> 00:46:10,825
Why not?

835
00:46:11,284 --> 00:46:12,827
Because I'd rather have
one for three!

836
00:46:16,831 --> 00:46:18,374
I also just read that online.

837
00:46:27,842 --> 00:46:28,676
I'm glad...

838
00:46:29,594 --> 00:46:31,054
I'm really glad you're here.

839
00:46:32,680 --> 00:46:35,558
It makes me feel a little less
nervous about the exhibit.

840
00:46:36,559 --> 00:46:37,602
You'll be there, okay?

841
00:46:38,686 --> 00:46:39,586
Of course.

842
00:46:39,937 --> 00:46:41,981
I just have something
to do in the morning,

843
00:46:41,981 --> 00:46:43,107
then I'll come right after.

844
00:46:43,733 --> 00:46:46,611
Of course, I won't miss
the masterpiece of...

845
00:46:46,611 --> 00:46:47,862
Ysabelle,

846
00:46:48,154 --> 00:46:49,113
Yeye,

847
00:46:49,113 --> 00:46:50,073
Bogart...

848
00:46:50,073 --> 00:46:53,117
Tristan, Lola Iska and Cacai.

849
00:46:54,160 --> 00:46:54,911
Right?

850
00:47:16,849 --> 00:47:17,892
Calm down.

851
00:47:18,601 --> 00:47:19,602
Calm down.

852
00:47:22,355 --> 00:47:23,398
Are you nervous, dear?

853
00:47:25,858 --> 00:47:27,016
Just a little bit.

854
00:47:28,027 --> 00:47:29,821
That's just normal, dear.

855
00:47:36,077 --> 00:47:37,829
It seems like you're waiting for someone.

856
00:47:38,663 --> 00:47:39,446
Uh...

857
00:47:40,289 --> 00:47:41,332
It's Estong.

858
00:47:41,916 --> 00:47:42,934
Oh.

859
00:47:42,959 --> 00:47:44,168
He's probably just stuck in traffic.

860
00:47:44,460 --> 00:47:45,670
He should be here soon.

861
00:47:46,504 --> 00:47:47,383
Ysa,

862
00:47:48,131 --> 00:47:49,465
try to stop worrying, okay?

863
00:47:49,465 --> 00:47:51,275
Focus on your event instead.

864
00:47:51,300 --> 00:47:52,593
Just enjoy it!

865
00:47:56,472 --> 00:47:58,307
Oh, guys!

866
00:47:58,307 --> 00:48:00,184
The show's about to start!

867
00:48:00,435 --> 00:48:01,602
Let's go inside!

868
00:48:02,061 --> 00:48:03,479
Let's go!

869
00:48:03,646 --> 00:48:05,891
I'm so excited!

870
00:48:09,735 --> 00:48:11,112
Ladies and gentlemen!

871
00:48:11,112 --> 00:48:14,907
Welcome to today's unveiling of the
new artist showcase!

872
00:48:17,410 --> 00:48:19,245
Are you guys ready?

873
00:48:19,245 --> 00:48:20,163
Ready!

874
00:48:20,163 --> 00:48:24,584
Okay, in three, two, one!

875
00:48:28,754 --> 00:48:29,964
Fabulous!

876
00:48:30,756 --> 00:48:32,300
Wonderful!

877
00:49:01,120 --> 00:49:03,372
Congratulations!

878
00:49:03,372 --> 00:49:06,959
You're amazing, dear. I told you so.

879
00:49:46,916 --> 00:49:47,797
Beautiful.

880
00:49:52,713 --> 00:49:53,548
Very beautiful.

881
00:49:57,593 --> 00:49:58,636
Sorry, I got stuck in traffic.

882
00:50:08,282 --> 00:50:09,722
Thank you, Estong.

883
00:50:11,508 --> 00:50:13,484
Thank you for the flowers, and...

884
00:50:15,111 --> 00:50:16,153
for your face.

885
00:50:21,450 --> 00:50:23,327
Ysabelle!

886
00:50:23,619 --> 00:50:26,289
I knew it! You belong here!

887
00:50:26,289 --> 00:50:28,165
Everybody loves it!

888
00:50:28,533 --> 00:50:30,017
Thanks so much again.

889
00:50:30,042 --> 00:50:31,165
You're welcome.

890
00:50:31,627 --> 00:50:32,837
Uh...

891
00:50:36,215 --> 00:50:37,758
That explains it.

892
00:50:38,009 --> 00:50:41,679
Looks like handsome gave the inspiration.

893
00:50:41,929 --> 00:50:43,139
So delicious!

894
00:50:44,473 --> 00:50:46,767
Well, anyway, I'll leave you two alone.

895
00:50:48,436 --> 00:50:49,829
Oh, he's really gorgeous!

896
00:50:49,854 --> 00:50:52,023
Well, anyway, I'll go now.

897
00:50:59,196 --> 00:51:00,406
Done at last.

898
00:51:04,285 --> 00:51:05,555
This is just the beginning.

899
00:51:08,456 --> 00:51:09,774
Congratulations, Ysa.

900
00:51:13,002 --> 00:51:14,462
Thanks again, Estong,

901
00:51:15,713 --> 00:51:17,298
for all your help.

902
00:51:18,424 --> 00:51:20,009
Thank you for the friendship.

903
00:51:22,261 --> 00:51:24,221
All of this would've been
impossible without you.

904
00:51:37,068 --> 00:51:38,527
Did I say anything wrong?

905
00:51:41,030 --> 00:51:41,739
No.

906
00:51:43,616 --> 00:51:44,659
But...

907
00:51:45,368 --> 00:51:46,577
I have something to say.

908
00:51:47,370 --> 00:51:48,829
I'm not sure if it's right.

909
00:51:50,831 --> 00:51:51,540
What is it?

910
00:51:52,249 --> 00:51:53,459
Congratulations, Ysa.

911
00:51:54,126 --> 00:51:54,877
Thank you.

912
00:51:59,799 --> 00:52:00,508
Ysa.

913
00:52:01,801 --> 00:52:02,843
What if...

914
00:52:03,511 --> 00:52:04,845
it gets to the point where...

915
00:52:08,224 --> 00:52:11,018
I'll start to like you
more than as a friend?

916
00:52:22,029 --> 00:52:22,919
Ysa?

917
00:52:31,455 --> 00:52:32,372
Ysa?

918
00:52:35,251 --> 00:52:36,460
Ysa, are you still there?

919
00:52:43,008 --> 00:52:44,301
Yes, Estong, I'm still here.

920
00:52:54,353 --> 00:52:55,646
But Estong, we can't.

921
00:53:00,401 --> 00:53:02,653
We can't be more than friends.

922
00:53:05,614 --> 00:53:07,324
You can't pursue me.

923
00:53:08,534 --> 00:53:10,077
We can never be together.

924
00:53:12,580 --> 00:53:14,165
You can't fall in love with me.

925
00:53:21,914 --> 00:53:22,891
I'm sorry.

926
00:53:23,966 --> 00:53:25,047
I'm sorry.

927
00:53:45,070 --> 00:53:46,739
That's what I've been saying.

928
00:53:46,989 --> 00:53:48,657
That Estong will fall for her.

929
00:53:48,783 --> 00:53:50,075
Is Ysa there?

930
00:53:50,242 --> 00:53:50,868
I just want to talk to her.

931
00:53:50,868 --> 00:53:53,596
No, you can't. I got her sick!

932
00:53:53,621 --> 00:53:56,081
We might start a pandemic.
You want to get sick too?

933
00:53:56,081 --> 00:53:57,008
Get out of here!

934
00:53:57,708 --> 00:53:58,667
Want to go to our café?

935
00:53:58,667 --> 00:54:00,711
- The air is fresh there—
- No!

936
00:54:00,961 --> 00:54:01,879
No!

937
00:54:01,879 --> 00:54:03,255
I don't like it there.

938
00:54:03,631 --> 00:54:04,482
No!

939
00:54:04,507 --> 00:54:05,352
Hey, you!

940
00:54:05,800 --> 00:54:06,884
What are you still doing here?

941
00:54:07,760 --> 00:54:08,511
You...

942
00:54:08,511 --> 00:54:11,547
back off and
stay away from Ysa!

943
00:54:11,639 --> 00:54:13,307
Don't worry, Ate.

944
00:54:13,307 --> 00:54:14,892
He'll eventually understand.

945
00:54:15,142 --> 00:54:17,061
I thought that whenever
you make a mistake...

946
00:54:17,561 --> 00:54:18,854
you have to erase it.

947
00:54:18,938 --> 00:54:20,815
Just because you made a mistake...

948
00:54:22,566 --> 00:54:24,235
doesn't mean erasing
it is the only solution.

949
00:54:25,319 --> 00:54:27,112
Don't worry, I understand.

950
00:54:27,279 --> 00:54:29,365
Thank you for
understanding, Estong.

951
00:54:29,740 --> 00:54:33,719
I've noticed there are things
you don't want to tell me.

952
00:54:33,744 --> 00:54:37,348
Maybe it's complicated but
whatever it is, I'll respect that.

953
00:54:37,373 --> 00:54:38,680
I won't push you.
